CTA: Discuss API Integration
H2: What Is a Forex Manager API?
MetaTrader 5 gives brokers several ways to connect external software to the trading server. The MT5 Manager API is one of the most widely used. It allows an application to perform many of the tasks a broker's staff would normally do through the Manager terminal, but programmatically, from your own systems.
In practical terms, that means your software can create and manage trading accounts, work with groups and symbols, process balance operations, retrieve positions, orders and deals, and receive trading data as it changes. MetaTrader 5 also offers other interfaces for different needs, such as a web-based API and server-side plugin development, and MT4 has its own manager interface for brokers still running that platform.
MetaTrader is developed by MetaQuotes. Access to these interfaces comes through your platform arrangement, and what's available depends on your setup. We design and build the integrations that use them, so your systems and your trading server work as one.
